[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we need to maximize the real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(z\) is a complex number with \(|z| = 4\). Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form: \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m First, we substitute \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\) into the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m (75 + 117i)z = (75 + 117i)4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta) = 4(75 \cos \theta + 75i \sin \theta + 117i \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) = 4(75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta + i (75 \sin \theta + 117 \cos \theta))
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos \theta - i \sin \theta)}{4(\cos^2 \theta + \sin^2 \theta)} = \frac{96 \cos \theta + 144 \sin \theta + i (144 \cos \theta - 96 \sin \theta)}{4} = 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta + i (36 \cos \theta - 24 \sin \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m Combining these, the expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m 4(75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta + i (75 \sin \theta + 117 \cos \theta)) + 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta + i (36 \cos \theta - 24 \sin \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m Separating the real and imaginary parts, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m \text{Real part} = 4(75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) + 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta = 300 \cos \theta - 468 \sin \theta + 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta = 324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m To maximize the real part, we need to maximize the expression \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\). This can be done by expressing it in the form \(R \cos(\theta + \phi)\), where \(R = \sqrt{324^2 + 432^2}\) and \(\tan \phi = \frac{432}{324} = \frac{4}{3}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m R = \sqrt{324^2 + 432^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 186624} = \sqrt{291600} = 540
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=68627)[0m The maximum value of \(R \cos(\theta + \phi)\) is \(R\), so the maximum value of the real part is \(540\). Therefore, the largest possible real part of the given expression is:
